From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: add sensor properties for the S5K5E3YX

Without an entry the sensor database logs

  No static properties available for 's5k5e3'

and the sensor's physical size is unknown, so nothing can turn the crop
rectangle into a field of view.

The S5K5E3YX is a 1/5" 5 Mpx sensor with a 1.12 um pixel pitch, over the
2576x1932 array the kernel driver reports.

No test pattern modes are listed: the driver does not register the sensor's
pattern menu, so there is nothing to map onto. Delays are left empty rather
than guessed, as they are for the other sensors here without a documented
pipeline depth.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
@@ -140,6 +140,11 @@
 			},
 			.sensorDelays = { },
 		} },
+		{ "s5k5e3", {
+			.unitCellSize = { 1120, 1120 },
+			.testPatternModes = { },
+			.sensorDelays = { },
+		} },
 		{ "hi846", {
 			.unitCellSize = { 1120, 1120 },
 			.testPatternModes = {
